SUMMARY:Cooks & Books: Baking Techniques & Equipment Swap
DESCRIPTION:Get your rolling pins ready! This month\, Cooks & Books is gett
 ing a head start on the festive season by focusing on baking techniques to
  help level up your holiday spread. To inspire your baking\, we’re drawi
 ng from two fantastic resources: Billy Parisi’s Website: Perfect for tho
 se who love detailed\, chef-driven techniques and classic methods. Chasing
  Flavors by Dan Kluger: A deep dive into how flavor profiles work to make 
 your bakes truly stand out. Bonus Special Event: We’ll also be hosting a
  Baking Tools & Equipment Swap! Bring any new or gently used kitchen gadge
 ts\, tools\, or baking supplies (like rolling pins\, specialty pans\, or d
 ecorative sprinkles) you'd like to trade with fellow home cooks. Cooks & B
 ooks is a welcoming space for anyone who loves food and cooking. Bring a d
 ish inspired by holiday baking techniques\, your own place setting/to-go c
 ontainer\, and a friend to join the conversation! Requirements: Attendees 
 should be 14 years of age or older. Vegan and vegetarian recipes are alway
 s welcome. Supplies: Please bring your own serving utensils\, place settin
 g\, to-go container\, and beverage. Cost: The event is free\, but reservat
 ions are required!\n\nPrice: Free\n\nSchedule listed: Mon\, Nov 02\, 2026 
 06:15 PM EST – Mon\, Nov 02\, 2026 07:45 PM EST\n\nSchedule supplied by 
 Lancaster Libraries\n\nTimes converted from America/New_York to UTC for ca
 lendar compatibility.\n\nRegistration: https://calendar.lancasterlibraries
 .org/event/hold-cooks-books-146704\n\nAdding this calendar item does not r
 egister you. Check the original listing for changes\; imported events do n
 ot automatically stay in sync.
